## Monorepo

- **Canonical source**: edit PHP, admin assets, languages, and `uninstall.php` under `packages/core/` only. Do not duplicate logic at the repo root except the dev bootstrap file.
- **Dev entry**: root `edminboost-admin-notice-manager.php` requires `packages/core/boot.php`, calls `edminboost_anm_register()` with `core_dir` / `core_url` pointing at `packages/core`, then `edminboost_anm_run_plugin()`.
- **Release editions**: `packages/free/` and `packages/pro/` each ship a thin bootstrap + `readme.txt`; build merges core + overlay into flat plugin trees under `dist/` (see `MONOREPO.md`, `build/config.json`).
- **Edition flags**: Free sets `EDMINBOOST_ANM_IS_PRO` false (slug `edminboost-admin-notice-manager`); Pro sets it true (slug `edminboost-admin-notice-manager-pro`). Gate Pro-only behavior with `edminboost_anm_is_pro()` (defined in `packages/core/load.php`).
- **Text domain**: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_TEXT_DOMAIN` is always `edminboost-admin-notice-manager` (shared `.pot` / locales under `packages/core/languages/`), even when `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_SLUG` is the Pro directory name.

## Architecture

- Edition bootstrap calls `edminboost_anm_register( $plugin_file, $edition )` in `packages/core/boot.php` — defines constants, sets `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_DIR` / `URL` to core (or assembled root), requires `load.php`, registers activation/deactivation on the edition main file. Then `edminboost_anm_run_plugin()` instantiates `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Plugin`. Loads `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Debug` only when `WP_DEBUG` is true.
- Edition main filename equals `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_SLUG . '.php'` (Free vs Pro bootstrap names differ).
- `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Plugin::run()` wires i18n, site + network admin menu/settings/assets, `wp_initialize_site` seeding, and on `init`: notices, interceptor, AJAX, digest, ad redirects (+ debug when loaded).
- **Options API only** — no custom database tables.
- **Stored options** (via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings` constants): `edminboost_anm_settings`, `edminboost_anm_rules`, `edminboost_anm_inbox`, `edminboost_anm_stats`, `edminboost_anm_version`. All seeded on activation with `autoload => false`.
- **Multisite sitemeta** (via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite`): `edminboost_anm_network` (policy), `edminboost_anm_network_settings` (default settings shape), `edminboost_anm_network_rules` (shared auto-rules). Seeded on network activation / first network admin visit; per-site options remain on each blog.
- Global kill switch: `enabled` in settings — toggled from Dashboard Quick Status (`edminboost_anm_toggle_enabled`); omitted from Settings form save (`sanitize()` preserves existing value when `enabled` is not posted). Tabbed Settings save preserves `upsell_preset` and `word_filters` when those keys are omitted from POST; digest/webhook sanitizers merge with stored values (`sanitize_digest_settings()`, `sanitize_webhook_settings()` — webhook URL kept when disabled or invalid posted URL).
- **AJAX**: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Ajax` — privileged `wp_ajax_*` actions (inbox list/sort, rules, capture, importer, user search, notice hide/reset hidden, digest preview, webhook preview, debug seeds) + `admin_post_edminboost_anm_export_rules`. Debug-only handlers use `verify_debug_request()`.
- **Inbox list UI**: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::parse_inbox_list_args()`, `get_inbox_list_slice()`, `render_inbox_table_rows_html()` — shared by inbox page and `edminboost_anm_inbox_list` AJAX.
- **Admin bar notice panel**: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Notices` — registers `admin_bar_menu` early; node and assets gated by `is_enabled()`, capability, and `should_show_admin_bar_notice_panel()` (`notice_panel.enabled` — always true after Settings save; no separate Settings toggle). Admin bar tab configures style, position, badge, and colors only. Styles `link`, `bell_link`, `dropdown`, `dropdown_compact`; positions via `get_notice_panel_admin_bar_placement()`. Dropdown uses `edminboost-anm-notice-panel-dropdown.php`. Live settings mock via `initNoticePanelPreview()`. Dropdown JS via `edminboost-anm-notices.js` when style is dropdown (wp-admin or front-end admin bar). Enqueues on `admin_enqueue_scripts` and `wp_enqueue_scripts`; `dashicons` when the live panel renders.
- **Inline notice actions**: `edminboost-anm-notice-inline.js` on non–plugin-screen wp-admin (capability required) — “Hide for me” / “Hide for all” on visible notices; uses `edminboost_anm_notice_hide` AJAX.
- **Plugin admin screens**: `get_plugin_screen_notice_hide_css()` (inline on `edminboost-anm-admin` + `admin_head` via `hide_notices_on_plugin_screens()`) and `initHidePluginAdminNotices()` (MutationObserver + `.edminboost-anm-notice-hidden`) hide stray notices; CSS re-shows mocks under `.edminboost-anm-display-experience-preview` / `.edminboost-anm-general-options-preview` / admin bar preview. `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Debug` clears queued live-test transients when entering a plugin screen.
- **Ad redirect blocker**: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Ad_Redirects` — when `block_ad_redirects.enabled`, blocks admin requests and `wp_redirect` targets matching user-configured URL patterns (admin-only; no external calls).
- **Cron**: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Digest` — weekly digest when enabled; registers custom `weekly` interval via `cron_schedules` (`CRON_SCHEDULE`); `CRON_HOOK` `edminboost_anm_weekly_digest`; `send_weekday` slug + site timezone (`SEND_HOUR`, default 9:00 local); `sync_schedule()` / `ensure_schedule_if_needed()` on save and `init`; `get_preview()` returns structured `content`, plain `body`, and `next_send` label. Customizable subject, intro, footer (`{site_name}` token), optional stats and recent inbox sections; cleared on deactivate/uninstall.
- **Multisite**: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite` — policies `per_site`, `network_defaults`, `network_locked`; optional site overrides for settings/rules; optional shared network auto-rules merged at runtime. Network admin: policy page, network default settings (reuses settings partial), network auto-rules (reuses rules partial with `rulesContext` `network`). Policy fields + next-steps markup shared via `edminboost-anm-multisite-policy-fields.php` and `edminboost-anm-multisite-policy-next-steps.php` (network policy page + site Settings **Multisite** tab). Site Settings adds **Multisite** tab (status + links) when multisite is active. `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::get()` merges network + site layers; locked policy uses network settings only. New sites: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::maybe_seed_new_site()` on `wp_initialize_site`.
- **Billing (plans UI)**: site admin submenu **Billing** — read-only Free vs Pro comparison table (`get_billing_comparison_rows()`, `render_billing_comparison_cell()`); upgrade link uses bootstrap constant `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PRO_URL`. Informational only — no license checks or feature gating in this plugin build (Pro separation is a follow-up).
- **White label**: `settings.white_label` — optional admin menu title, dashboard brand/logo, hide brand/docs, custom docs URL; `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::sanitize_white_label_settings()`; menu/docs helpers for admin UI.
- **Rules**: match types `keyword`, `regex`, `css` — `html_matches_css_selector()` for class/id/tag.class on notice HTML; upsell suppression via `get_active_blacklist_phrases()` (custom phrases always; built-in preset when enabled). Site rules CRUD respects `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::site_can_edit_rules()`; network rules stored separately and merged when `share_network_rules` is on.
- **Inbox**: snooze 1d/7d with toggle unsnooze (same duration or Snooze control) via `edminboost_anm_inbox_action`; `snooze_duration` key on stored notices; Read marks row and disables button (`is-read`).
- **External requests**: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Webhook::maybe_send()` posts JSON via `build_payload()` to a user-configured URL only when webhook is enabled (opt-in). Custom `text` template supports tokens (`{source}`, `{message}`, `{message_excerpt}`, `{type}`, `{site}`, `{site_name}`). Settings preview via `get_preview()` uses latest non-archived inbox notice or `get_sample_notice()`. No telemetry or vendor tracking.
- **Inbox query**: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Inbox::query()` applies `page` / `per_page` slicing after sort/filter (used by digest recent section and list UI).
- Admin UI: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin` + partials (`help_tip( $message, $placement )` — dashicon tips with `data-tip` / optional `data-tip-placement` `below`|`left`). Settings page: tabbed sections (General, Notices, Access, Admin bar, Filtering, Security & Shield, Notifications, White label, Migration; plus **Multisite** on multisite sites); General two-column live previews; White label live preview; digest + webhook previews on Notifications; redirect blocklist on Security. Read-only settings form (`.is-settings-readonly`) when network policy blocks site edits. `is_plugin_screen()` matches `$_GET['page']` when needed; network screens via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::is_network_plugin_screen()`. Plugins row meta Docs link respects white-label settings.
- Plugin-screen assets via `is_plugin_screen()` or `is_network_plugin_screen()` (inbox/settings enqueue `list-tables` + `dashicons`). Notice CSS on wp-admin when plugin enabled; also on front-end admin bar when panel active for capable users. Inline hide JS on wp-admin outside plugin screens. Dropdown panel JS (`edminboost-anm-notices`) for dropdown styles when panel is shown. Interceptor JS on all wp-admin when plugin enabled (includes `network_admin_notices`). Dashboard Quick Status toggle reloads after AJAX save when `site_can_edit_settings()`.

## Admin Pages

Use `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin::PAGE_SLUG` (equals `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_SLUG`).

| Page | Slug | Renderer |
|------|------|----------|
| Dashboard | `PAGE_SLUG` | `render_dashboard_page()` |
| Inbox | `PAGE_SLUG . '-inbox'` | `render_inbox_page()` |
| Rules | `PAGE_SLUG . '-rules'` | `render_rules_page()` |
| Settings | `PAGE_SLUG . '-settings'` | `render_settings_page()` |
| Billing | `PAGE_SLUG . '-billing'` | `render_billing_page()` |

**Network admin** (multisite only; capability `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::NETWORK_CAPABILITY` — `manage_network_options`):

| Page | Slug | Renderer |
|------|------|----------|
| Multisite policy | `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::NETWORK_PAGE_SLUG` | `render_network_policy_page()` |
| Network defaults | `NETWORK_SETTINGS_PAGE_SLUG` | `render_network_defaults_page()` (settings partial) |
| Network Auto-Rules | `NETWORK_PAGE_SLUG . '-rules'` | `render_network_rules_page()` (rules partial) |

Site admin capability: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::CAPABILITY` (`manage_options`).

Settings constants: `OPTION_NAME`, `RULES_OPTION`, `INBOX_OPTION`, `STATS_OPTION`, `VERSION_OPTION`, `SETTINGS_GROUP`. Multisite: `NETWORK_OPTION`, `NETWORK_SETTINGS_OPTION`, `NETWORK_RULES_OPTION`, policy/settings API groups on `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite`.

## Naming

Project prefix: `edminboost_anm` (use `edminboost-anm` in slugs/handles). Distinct from main EdminBoost plugin (`EDMINBOOST_*` without `_ANM`).

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Constants | `EDMINBOOST_ANM_*` | `EDMINBOOST_ANM_VERSION` |
| Plugin slug (edition) | `edminboost-admin-notice-manager` or `…-pro` | `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_SLUG` |
| Text domain (shared) | `edminboost-admin-notice-manager` | `EDMINBOOST_ANM_TEXT_DOMAIN` |
| Classes | `EDMINBOOST_ANM_{Name}` | `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Admin` |
| Functions | `edminboost_anm_{action}` | `edminboost_anm_run_plugin()` |
| Options | `edminboost_anm_{key}` | `edminboost_anm_inbox` |
| CSS/JS handles | `edminboost-anm-{name}` | `edminboost-anm-interceptor` |
| CSS classes | `edminboost-anm-*` | `edminboost-anm-wrap` |
| JS global (localized) | `edminboostAnmData` | plugin screens + interceptor |
| AJAX nonce action | `edminboost_anm_admin` | via `get_localized_data()` |

`EDMINBOOST_ANM_TEXT_DOMAIN` is fixed across editions; do not tie it to the Pro plugin slug.

## Extension Hooks

- `edminboost_anm_settings_defaults` — filter default settings
- `edminboost_anm_settings` — filter merged settings on read
- `edminboost_anm_sanitize_settings` — filter sanitized settings on save
- `edminboost_anm_notices_loaded` — after notice manager hooks register
- `edminboost_anm_upsell_preset_phrases` — filter built-in upsell phrase list
- `edminboost_anm_wp_notice_presets` — filter WordPress core notice preset definitions (Rules page)
- `edminboost_anm_digest_email` — filter digest subject/body before send or preview
- `edminboost_anm_webhook_payload` — filter outbound webhook JSON payload
- `edminboost_anm_billing_comparison` — filter Free vs Pro rows on the Billing page
- `edminboost_anm_block_ad_redirect_activation_flags` — filter activation option suppressors when block ad redirects is enabled

## Scope & Change Discipline

- Admin-only plugin — limited front-end hooks for admin bar notice panel assets when the toolbar is visible.
- Minimize diff scope; match existing file structure and coding style.
- Add `index.php` silence files when creating new directories.
- Update `packages/free/readme.txt` (and `packages/pro/readme.txt` when Pro copy differs) changelog for user-facing changes; run `npm run build` before shipping zips from `dist/zips/`.
- Update `packages/core/uninstall.php` when adding new stored options or cron hooks (include multisite sitemeta in `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::uninstall_all_sites()` when applicable).
- Keep `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/` aligned when architecture or workflows change.

## Constants (use, don't redefine)

`EDMINBOOST_ANM_VERSION`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_IS_PRO`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_FILE`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_DIR`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_URL`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_BASENAME`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_SLUG`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_TEXT_DOMAIN`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PLUGIN_DOCS_URL`, `EDMINBOOST_ANM_PRO_URL`
